1) To convert any local repo/directory  into git repo
 -> git init 
2) To clone remote files into our local machine/editor
 -> git clone https://github.com/janaaloke4/test-repo.git
3) in terminal inorder to move next folder we use below command 
 -> cd <filename>
4) To view all the available file inside the repo we use below command
-> ls
5) To Check if there is/are any changes between our local repo and remote repo, 
 -> git status
 ---- Type of git status --------------( File change cycle: Add new changes -> Add/stagging area -> commit ) 
	1) Untracked :  new files that git doesnt yet track, ex: we created a new file in our local repo which not yet push into remote file
	2) modified  :  This status appear when we made any new changes on the existing file, but not yet pushed into remote file
	3) staged	 :  This appear when file is ready tobe committed ( Before commit)

6) To move our changes into stagged state 
 -> git add <fileName>  // Single file 
 -> git add .           // Add all changes at once
 
7) Once we add our changes it is now ready to commit.
 -> git commit -m "<Add your commit message >"
 
8) To upload local repo content into remote repo we have to push our chnages , then only it will visable in the remote side.
 -> git push origin main
 
 // Here 'origin' - meaning our remote repo name
 // 'main' -  meaning our branch name, now if you want to puch changes on other branch the need to replace 'main' with that branch name.
 ....................................... Branch ...............................................

9) To check on which branch we are working
 -> git branch
10) To rename any branch 
 -> git branch -M <New Name>
11) To check on which remote repo we are currently working 
 -> git remote -v
12) To create a new branch 
 -> git checkout -b <new branch name>
13) To move one branch to another 
-> git checkout <next branch name>
14) To delete any branch. // note that, we cant delete branch, if we are on the same branch. ex, if we are in branch B1 then cant delete B1
 -> git branch -d <name of that branch which you want to delete>